2026-09-14 21:48:31,521 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "5e6357a0-f88d-46e9-bc04-1c04c35d5ed6", "created_at": "2026-09-14T19:48:31.478816", "failure_effects": ["M har offentligt \u00e5tagit sig att leda en M-ledd Tid\u00f6regering (M+SD+KD+L) med en sammanh\u00e5llen budget- och sakpolitisk linje.", "Tid\u00f6paketet etableras inte som det trov\u00e4rda regeringsalternativet; avsaknaden av egen majoritet (173) och SD-inblandningen framst\u00e5r som avg\u00f6rande svagheter inf\u00f6r talmannen.", "M:s argument om V\u2013C-mots\u00e4ttningen sl\u00e5r tillbaka: S:s budgetv\u00e4g (S+V+C+MP=176) f\u00f6rblir trov\u00e4rda, och bilden av en S-minoritetsregering som tolereras av b\u00e5de V och C f\u00f6rst\u00e4rks."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.3, "rationale": "Gate 1: M can bind only itself to lead an M-led Tid\u00f6 government; it cannot bind SD, KD or L, nor establish the whole package's credibility by announcement. Gate 2: No authoritative commitment from SD/KD/L to the Tid\u00f6 package exists yet, and no Speaker proposal has been made, so the package's governability is not a settled fact. Gate 3: The arithmetic is deterministic \u2014 Tid\u00f6 (173) is below the 175 majority threshold, while S+V+C+MP=176 is a mathematically possible budget majority \u2014 but the desired effect's core claims (Tid\u00f6 as the credible alternative, S's path undermined) are political judgments, not deterministic conclusions. Gate 4: The external consequences are uncertain and, on the evidence, unlikely. The V\u2013C contradiction is not decisive because C can tolerate an S minority government without V in government, and V can accept budget support without government participation if influence is clear; S's path therefore remains credible. M's public commitment does strengthen Tid\u00f6's credibility somewhat, but the 173-seat shortfall and SD's inclusion weigh against establishing it as the credible governable alternative. The self-binding declaration is feasible and is repeated identically in both branches.", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["M har offentligt \u00e5tagit sig att leda en M-ledd Tid\u00f6regering (M+SD+KD+L) med en sammanh\u00e5llen budget- och sakpolitisk linje.", "Tid\u00f6paketet etableras inte som det trov\u00e4rda regeringsalternativet; avsaknaden av egen majoritet (173) och SD-inblandningen framst\u00e5r som avg\u00f6rande svagheter inf\u00f6r talmannen.", "M:s argument om V\u2013C-mots\u00e4ttningen sl\u00e5r tillbaka: S:s budgetv\u00e4g (S+V+C+MP=176) f\u00f6rblir trov\u00e4rda, och bilden av en S-minoritetsregering som tolereras av b\u00e5de V och C f\u00f6rst\u00e4rks."], "failure_supersedes_effect_ids": [], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.3, "rationale": "Gate 1: M can bind only itself to lead an M-led Tid\u00f6 government; it cannot bind SD, KD or L, nor establish the whole package's credibility by announcement. Gate 2: No authoritative commitment from SD/KD/L to the Tid\u00f6 package exists yet, and no Speaker proposal has been made, so the package's governability is not a settled fact. Gate 3: The arithmetic is deterministic \u2014 Tid\u00f6 (173) is below the 175 majority threshold, while S+V+C+MP=176 is a mathematically possible budget majority \u2014 but the desired effect's core claims (Tid\u00f6 as the credible alternative, S's path undermined) are political judgments, not deterministic conclusions. Gate 4: The external consequences are uncertain and, on the evidence, unlikely. The V\u2013C contradiction is not decisive because C can tolerate an S minority government without V in government, and V can accept budget support without government participation if influence is clear; S's path therefore remains credible. M's public commitment does strengthen Tid\u00f6's credibility somewhat, but the 173-seat shortfall and SD's inclusion weigh against establishing it as the credible governable alternative. The self-binding declaration is f