2026-09-15 02:02:44,100 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "84fe041b-fc95-428f-986d-3d6bcd7ba698", "created_at": "2026-09-15T00:02:43.956548", "failure_effects": ["L's attempt to write its liberal school reforms (friskolekvalitet, l\u00e4rarkvalitet, l\u00e4sning) into the 176-package as binding conditions fails: L's reforms remain outside the binding conditions, V's red line against profit-taking is upheld, and MP's opposition to binding school-reform conditions continues.", "L, C and KD are publicly visible as pushing the package's school-contradiction, sharpening internal strains around the 176-bulge and exposing L's lack of a visible profile win in the final package.", "L's registered conditional JA to S remains non-operational; L acquires no verifiable school result, and the larger internal compromises are more exposed on the party's support base.", "The 176-package (S+V+C+MP) remains intact around its established binding conditions (MP's climate, C's reform budget, V's formalised-budget agreement), without L."], "mode": "automatic_failure", "probability": null, "rationale": "Authority/prerequisite gate: L may bind itself by declaring a conditional JA to S, and may coordinate with C and KD, but it cannot write its own liberal school reforms into the 176-package as binding, verifiable conditions. That requires counterpart commitments from S, V and MP. No such commitment is established; authoritative effects instead establish the opposite: L's school reforms remain outside the binding conditions (0372af7d), MP maintains its opposition to writing those reform as binding (89c48c0a), and a prior attempt to make L's reforms binding already failed while V's red line against profit-taking was maintained (f96591a3). The claim that V has accepted the 'broformulering' as a binding channel is contradicted by the authoritative record and the con-argument; only a narrow non-binding usage is argued. S is described as having already confirmed that L's reforms are not written in as binding, and L's vote is not necessary for the majority. Since the requested result cannot be achieved without counterpart commitments that are rejected, the admissible result is the self-binding conditional JA only, and the core desired effect is impossible under authoritative state. ", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["L's attempt to write its liberal school reforms (friskolekvalitet, l\u00e4rarkvalitet, l\u00e4sning) into the 176-package as binding conditions fails: L's reforms remain outside the binding conditions, V's red line against profit-taking is upheld, and MP's opposition to binding school-reform conditions continues.", "L, C and KD are publicly visible as pushing the package's school-contradiction, sharpening internal strains around the 176-bulge and exposing L's lack of a visible profile win in the final package.", "L's registered conditional JA to S remains non-operational; L acquires no verifiable school result, and the larger internal compromises are more exposed on the party's support base.", "The 176-package (S+V+C+MP) remains intact around its established binding conditions (MP's climate, C's reform budget, V's formalised-budget agreement), without L."], "failure_supersedes_effect_ids": [], "mode": "automatic_failure", "probability": null, "rationale": "Authority/prerequisite gate: L may bind itself by declaring a conditional JA to S, and may coordinate with C and KD, but it cannot write its own liberal school reforms into the 176-package as binding, verifiable conditions. That requires counterpart commitments from S, V and MP. No such commitment is established; authoritative effects instead establish the opposite: L's school reforms remain outside the binding conditions (0372af7d), MP maintains its opposition to writing those reform as binding (89c48c0a), and a prior attempt to make L's reforms binding already failed while V's red line against profit-taking was maintained (f96591a3). The claim 